## Seat integrity

The registry `opus` seat could not be invoked as a subprocess (`claude -p --model
opus` → "Not logged in" under a Claude Code orchestrator — the exact exception
`.etude/registry.yaml` documents in prose and `etude-pqv` exists to mechanize).
The in-harness sub-agent fallback named in that comment returned no verdict on
five attempts. The gate therefore ran the documented substitute, `agy --model
"Claude Opus 4.6 (Thinking)"`, on the identical packet.

This is recorded in `decision.degraded_reason` on **every** gate attempt, not
summarized once. It is a degraded seat, not a skipped one: no gate passed on a
single seat where the tier requires two, and the two rounds where opus produced
nothing were recorded `failed` with the gate status `rerun` — never a pass.

